text:
recent patient; had EVLT both legs;
the clinic is well setup and operates smoothly; good staff;
dr kittipan , educated overseas, speaks perfect english and has heard and answered all your questions many times; my surgery was done right at the clinic; the fee structures are presented and are quite clear;  surgery was done on the 2nd floor in what amounts to an operating room;

dr kittipan explained everything well beforehand and also as the operation was progressing;
dr kittipan responds well and promptly to questions, either online or in person, a true professional; he is good at what he does;

imo, worth your excellent choice to choose him and his clinic;
clinic is relatively easy to find, parking not great and not awful either; clinic is very well marked and close off to a main road;

my consultation was saturday morning and the surgery done that afternoon, no overnight stay necessary anywhere;

note: the compression stockings Do have to be worn post operation for a couple weeks but not for the rest of your life; they provide them and even help you get them on ( never very easy);
to make things go smoothly make an appt ahead , i attended my prior-scheduled (appt + surgery) on a saturday;

note: initially i was having problems with only one leg but ultrasounds at the clinic showed issues with both legs; was only a matter of time before the other leg would act up ( and the fee schedule is pretty "2-leg-friendly" )

highly recommended
